Copyright 2026 ezzabuzaid

This package is a TypeScript port of parts of MTEB (Massive Text Embedding
Benchmark), version 2.26.28, https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/mteb,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). The ported files
were changed: docs/ported-from-mteb.md lists each source module and each
difference.

It also ports the semantics of parts of these dependencies of MTEB:

- pytrec_eval (terrierteam/pytrec_eval 0.5.11), Copyright (c) 2017 Christophe
  Van Gysel, MIT License, and the trec_eval measures that it binds
  (https://github.com/usnistgov/trec_eval).
- NumPy 2.5.4 (sum, mean, standard deviation, add.reduceat, stable argsort,
  linspace, corrcoef, quantile, the sum of float32 values, the mean of
  float32 values and along an axis, the MT19937 generator, randint,
  random_sample, choice, permutation and shuffle of the legacy RandomState,
  and the PCG64 generator, integers, shuffle, permutation and choice without
  replacement of default_rng, and the file layout of a float32 np.memmap),
  Copyright (c) NumPy Developers, BSD 3-Clause License. The pairwise summation of float64 values
  is the npm dependency @stdlib/blas-ext-base-gsumpw, Copyright (c) The Stdlib
  Authors, Apache License 2.0. The package does not include its code.
- scikit-learn 1.9.1 (sklearn.metrics.auc and average_precision_score,
  paired_cosine_distances, paired_euclidean_distances,
  paired_manhattan_distances, normalize, row_norms, v_measure_score,
  adjusted_mutual_info_score, MiniBatchKMeans, accuracy_score, f1_score,
  precision_score, recall_score, LogisticRegression with the lbfgs solver,
  KNeighborsClassifier, MultiLabelBinarizer,
  label_ranking_average_precision_score, LinearRegression,
  mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error and r2_score), Copyright (c) scikit-learn
  developers, BSD 3-Clause License.
- scikit-multilearn (the iterative stratification, which MTEB copies in
  mteb/abstasks/_stratification.py), Copyright (c) Piotr Szymański and
  contributors, BSD 2-Clause License.
- SciPy 1.18.1 (scipy.stats.rankdata, pearsonr, spearmanr and kendalltau,
  scipy.linalg.lstsq, and
  scipy.special.gammaln, the lgam of Cephes by Stephen L. Moshier, and
  scipy.optimize.minimize with L-BFGS-B: lbfgsb.c, the C port of L-BFGS-B 3.0
  by Ciyou Zhu, Richard Byrd, Peihuang Lu and Jorge Nocedal, with dcsrch and
  dcstep of MINPACK-2), Copyright (c) 2001-2002 Enthought, Inc. 2003, SciPy
  Developers, BSD 3-Clause License.
- packaging 26.3 (packaging.version), Copyright (c) Donald Stufft and
  individual contributors, Apache License 2.0 or BSD 2-Clause License.
- CPython 3.12 (the float sum, round, repr, format and heapq algorithms,
  random.Random, the repr, strip and splitlines of a str, and the order of a
  set of ints), Copyright (c) Python Software Foundation, PSF License
  Agreement.
- bm25s 0.3.16 (tokenize and the BM25 variants Robertson, Lucene, ATIRE,
  BM25L and BM25+), Copyright (c) 2024 Xing Han Lu, MIT License.
- PyStemmer 3.1.0 (Stemmer.Stemmer), Copyright (c) 2006 Richard Boulton, MIT
  License.
- pandas 3.1.0 (DataFrame, explode, pivot_table, the groupby mean, to_csv,
  to_markdown, to_latex and qcut), Copyright (c) 2008-2011 AQR Capital Management,
  LLC, Lambda Foundry, Inc. and PyData Development Team, and 2011-2026 Open
